# File Naming Conventions

## Python Files

- Use lowercase with underscores: `implementations.py`, `problems.py`, `examples.py`
- Test files: `test_<module_or_topic>.py` (e.g. `test_main.py`, `test_arrays.py`)
- Keep names descriptive; follow patterns in README and CONTRIBUTING

## Module Folders

- Format: `##_descriptive_name/` (e.g. `02_arrays_and_strings/`, `07_hashing_and_problem_patterns/`)
- Number 01–07 for the seven curriculum modules

## Documentation Files

- In modules: `notes.md`, `theory.md`, `concepts.md`
- In docs/: descriptive names; number when order matters (e.g. `01_abstract.md`)

## Configuration Files

- `pyproject.toml`: Project and tool config (pytest, black, coverage)
- `.python-version`: Python version (3.12)
- `requirements.txt`: Optional pip install list (see CONTRIBUTING)
